// A shift distance the checker cannot see is checked at RUN time, with the same message. It has to be
// checked somewhere: LLVM leaves a shift by 64 or more undefined, and on x86 the hardware masks the
// distance to six bits — so `x << 64` would silently answer x.
//
// Both compilers report this byte for byte, which is the differential's job.
function shifty(x: Int, n: Int) -> Int {
    return shift_left(x, n);
}
print(shifty(1, 10));
print(shifty(1, 64));
